            <ArticleTitle>Mitral valve endocarditis resulting from coagulase-negative Staphylococcus after stent implantation in a saphenous vein graft.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>152-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Valvular endocarditis after percutaneous coronary intervention is unusual. We report a new case of mitral valve endocarditis after stent implantation to a saphenous vein graft.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
